From: Mayank Mohan <18081415+mayankmohan1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/gud: bound the TV mode loop so FORTIFY accepts it at -O3

gud_connector_add_tv_mode() derives num_modes from the length of the GUD reply
and then walks both modes[] (GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM entries) and a buffer
of GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM * GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN bytes with
that value. The runtime invariant ret <= buf_len - the reply is capped by the
buffer length handed to gud_usb_get() - is invisible to the compiler, so since
upstream commit da1ea35fea67 ("drm/gud: validate TV mode names before creating
enum property") the fortified memchr() in that loop is a provable out-of-bounds
read for the optimizer, and clang 22 at -O3 rejects it:

  ld.lld: error: call to __read_overflow marked "dontcall-error": detected
  read beyond size of object (1st parameter)

Without LTO the same thing is reported by the front end instead:

  include/linux/fortify-string.h:686:3: error: call to '__read_overflow'
  declared with 'error' attribute: detected read beyond size of object

Reject replies that claim more modes than the protocol defines - which also keeps
drm_mode_create_tv_properties_legacy() from walking uninitialised modes[] entries
- and make the loop bound explicit. Both parts are needed: the check alone still
trips the trap, and the bound alone would leave the property creation reading
modes[] past the number of valid entries.

Verified with this package's default build options (clang 22.1.8, ThinLTO,
CONFIG_FORTIFY_SOURCE=y, KBUILD_CFLAGS -O3, CONFIG_DRM_GUD=m): the patched tree
builds drivers/gpu/drm/gud/ clean, the unpatched tree fails with the ld.lld error
above, and GCC -O3 (LTO=none) builds clean before and after.

Carry as a local workaround until an equivalent bound lands upstream.

Link: https://github.com/CachyOS/linux-cachyos/issues/1031
Signed-off-by: Mayank Mohan <18081415+mayankmohan1992@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
@@ -396,7 +396,12 @@
 	}
 
 	num_modes = ret / GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN;
-	for (i = 0; i < num_modes; i++) {
+	if (num_modes > GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM) {
+		ret = -EIO;
+		goto free;
+	}
+
+	for (i = 0; i < num_modes && i < GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM; i++) {
 		char *mode = &buf[i * GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN];
 
 		if (!memchr(mode, '\0', GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN)) {
